## 4. Enhanced Accessibility & Inclusion

### **Universal Design Principles**
- **WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance:** Full accessibility for users with disabilities
- **Keyboard Navigation:** Complete functionality without mouse
- **Screen Reader Optimization:** Semantic HTML with proper ARIA labels
- **High Contrast Mode:** Support for users with visual impairments
- **Font Scaling:** Support for up to 200% zoom without loss of functionality
- **Motion Sensitivity:** Respect for users' motion preferences

### **Global Accessibility**
- **Multi-language Support:** 20+ languages with professional translations
- **RTL Text Support:** Full support for right-to-left languages
- **Cultural Sensitivity:** Culturally appropriate imagery and content
- **Economic Accessibility:** Works on low-end devices and slow networks
- **Offline Capability:** Core functionality available offline
- **Progressive Enhancement:** Works without JavaScript for basic functionality

### **Inclusive Design**
- **Diverse Imagery:** Representative imagery from all cultures and backgrounds
- **Inclusive Language:** Gender-neutral and culturally sensitive language
- **Multiple Learning Styles:** Visual, auditory, and kinesthetic learning options
- **Economic Sensitivity:** Pricing and messaging appropriate for all economic levels
- **Technology Agnostic:** Works across all devices and browsers

